  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 3.2239166666666668,
      "text": "Imagine a measuring strip that keeps zooming in.",
      "source_sha256": "dcaa0064b3edeeea388cf9505cc99e807eb6826ec95e4bba755a634340685300"
    },
    {
      "start": 3.343916666666667,
      "end": 7.634666666666667,
      "text": "First we see little parts, then even smaller parts inside those.",
      "source_sha256": "2fa820994be3f57fad01cb26daef652a67c4f947a425f9aa08a3b37a1ab84c36"
    },
    {
      "start": 7.754666666666667,
      "end": 10.521833333333333,
      "text": "How can we name an amount precisely?",
      "source_sha256": "75fdd15b78c0c2ef3793d3fab166dd66d2162949e99c8c002e41c14d9b62cc63"
    },
    {
      "start": 10.641833333333333,
      "end": 14.370125,
      "text": "Our place-value pattern has a wonderfully useful answer.",
      "source_sha256": "153adcdf985e27bc2b7555c467850b646a8b4ef73b1dd04b61aa9c3d52a71bba"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.733333333333333,
      "end": 19.506166666666665,
      "text": "Today, we’re learning to explain decimal place value through thousandths.",
      "source_sha256": "dea8020f8e7298711ff1f99448e50aa281bbfd8cbb2ad92115dd572f2bee77a8"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.866666666666667,
      "end": 23.320875,
      "text": "You’ll be able to name tenths, hundredths and thousandths.",
      "source_sha256": "4f216419872cb5b5077cfd8dbda581ada7045274a930bde0f72f35ea91600abb"
    },
    {
      "start": 23.7,
      "end": 28.894708333333334,
      "text": "You’ll be able to give a decimal digit’s value and write a number in expanded form.",
      "source_sha256": "8bfd1892a8ffc47f2c3bf3c579594d00ed74bd74882b4c6b17f835b2db2321ea"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.266666666666666,
      "end": 34.309041666666666,
      "text": "You’ll be able to explain the ten-times relationship between neighbouring places.",
      "source_sha256": "e03b293ab2624d06adc4227d359b3e8a9b5c6b920ec6bedaba70db07827ddf02"
    },
    {
      "start": 34.666666666666664,
      "end": 38.8,
      "text": "What happens when we split one whole into smaller equal parts?",
      "source_sha256": "c3fcca66b17b4096d7c876deaee020f657038c7d386622dc67e8640fe2eb5f07"
    },
    {
      "start": 38.92,
      "end": 42.986875,
      "text": "The same base ten pattern continues beyond the decimal point.",
      "source_sha256": "51c645573b762d629218f479a7200bfd62744f7fc11842280f93fe13fbe2df5d"
    },
    {
      "start": 43.106875,
      "end": 46.52220833333333,
      "text": "After ones come tenths, hundredths and thousandths.",
      "source_sha256": "f84d02f77c295ba135e0f3fb31bf2acba12ea84c6d7510557f55e80ab007a441"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.642208333333336,
      "end": 51.43320833333333,
      "text": "Each place is one tenth of the value of the place immediately to its left.",
      "source_sha256": "212677b23b639b9f951c144a5f0f1cd08f8e48f36649f5800f0bba8b23c4b625"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.8,
      "end": 55.368291666666664,
      "text": "Before we name each part, predict the value of the seven.",
      "source_sha256": "32dce45a4070b3cb78b195d7bdcd913a7bab4c35033436533b00f05376476120"
    },
    {
      "start": 55.48829166666667,
      "end": 59.099666666666664,
      "text": "Is it seven wholes, seven tenths, or seven hundredths?",
      "source_sha256": "e9a0ff5b049c71e0aec342fa85d3bfe3e9b8945d5d7034f75eefecea34d25ad6"
    },
    {
      "start": 60.6,
      "end": 63.186875,
      "text": "Read four point seven two six.",
      "source_sha256": "56e20290d6b1efc003e7723f2f835d324c16090a306876c3c85eddeb51197f6d"
    },
    {
      "start": 63.306875,
      "end": 65.216875,
      "text": "The four is four ones.",
      "source_sha256": "d03975215184defc9e4220ca4d16c7cb42d588befc43c4f842cfc7d8c8e970a8"
    },
    {
      "start": 65.336875,
      "end": 69.15795833333334,
      "text": "The seven is seven tenths, written zero point seven.",
      "source_sha256": "e83d7622b307df5dd61be04e697374aaef94c7af2551fd8b5f2ab5bb52cb6269"
    },
    {
      "start": 69.27795833333333,
      "end": 73.144125,
      "text": "The two is two hundredths, written zero point zero two.",
      "source_sha256": "8a43d5668cc968dbc868c5a2f356e8239a1f87d584933c266b7ea3f8d71b64a6"
    },
    {
      "start": 73.264125,
      "end": 77.78333333333333,
      "text": "The six is six thousandths, written zero point zero zero six.",
      "source_sha256": "d89e19c1bd14fe5b239926112e25283776768deace67d234d917b123c7af5f54"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.13333333333334,
      "end": 79.76225,
      "text": "Put the parts together.",
      "source_sha256": "c77cd9b2274365e2d5679d211f835c4fbc5725d40dfa62c8da7b1f574c33a5f6"
    },
    {
      "start": 79.88225,
      "end": 88.62279166666667,
      "text": "Four point seven two six equals four, plus zero point seven, plus zero point zero two, plus zero point zero zero six.",
      "source_sha256": "707f75cd5a08ac1008373d1e06e9850586cadc225c759d076c49e057f315a457"
    },
    {
      "start": 88.74279166666666,
      "end": 95.862125,
      "text": "The digits describe different sized parts, so their positions matter just as much as they do in whole numbers.",
      "source_sha256": "66280f4ab1498be1e864abe6c01a2d5f11cd9893ea6f9b110064b2f8b4cdc36f"
    },
    {
      "start": 96.23333333333333,
      "end": 99.20458333333333,
      "text": "The digit five appears in both numbers.",
      "source_sha256": "5f5fc276fd3c97bab4653c7009185bf450a27c68e150f32523851f15d5dce814"
    },
    {
      "start": 99.32458333333334,
      "end": 102.003625,
      "text": "Do you think these two amounts are equal?",
      "source_sha256": "0e7814ba1dfca51feda8362711cccb48a4e1b78c71fc11cfc79901a657ed02c6"
    },
    {
      "start": 102.123625,
      "end": 105.23558333333334,
      "text": "Picture tenths and hundredths before deciding.",
      "source_sha256": "ba7fb615575ea197354e92e5df6ef8cfcaf43a86a2a2f0b13f2712371443a428"
    },
    {
      "start": 106.76666666666667,
      "end": 109.02633333333333,
      "text": "A tenth is ten hundredths.",
      "source_sha256": "3177a5ccc1e87cad050ce5f45730c8fbdc553ea46e9faa90a7c1d3078e9ae5c0"
    },
    {
      "start": 109.14633333333333,
      "end": 111.70245833333334,
      "text": "A hundredth is ten thousandths.",
      "source_sha256": "6868126130031291619eebdcd03ec0f7a53b76cd15322b048bda469a129dc57d"
    },
    {
      "start": 111.82245833333333,
      "end": 116.13504166666667,
      "text": "Now compare zero point five with zero point zero five.",
      "source_sha256": "24ae03e898051a5eac660af3b7e80c5f1fd7da7321b04c799be2df9248dab023"
    },
    {
      "start": 116.25504166666667,
      "end": 121.36825,
      "text": "Five tenths is ten times five hundredths, so zero point five is greater.",
      "source_sha256": "367c56ea3962dd92d1a70d2ab87827550fb4666ff06f946dff86eb4283e8bb3d"
    },
    {
      "start": 121.48825,
      "end": 124.45941666666667,
      "text": "The same digit does not mean the same value.",
      "source_sha256": "7753fa409af861c5884c84dcc12084a97116a06914361a24cca67ce00383b183"
    },
    {
      "start": 124.83333333333333,
      "end": 128.74908333333335,
      "text": "Think of a measuring scale marked in equal small steps.",
      "source_sha256": "0e1ed828ff17e48943e0375fb352ce7b127cab90fed3327039b4f6f53b142dd4"
    },
    {
      "start": 128.86908333333332,
      "end": 133.6225,
      "text": "Thousandths let us describe positions more precisely than hundredths.",
      "source_sha256": "6e788c842eba939135235709757a4f4f477c15b1f9e9feb51ab1e25cf9bdf151"
    },
    {
      "start": 133.7425,
      "end": 139.94695833333333,
      "text": "This is about understanding place value, not just counting how many digits come after the point.",
      "source_sha256": "e172679a48727d04ded86ad04610a24c452f0a4eccf1f83bfcd24f2ad6f8fdb7"
    },
    {
      "start": 140.06695833333333,
      "end": 143.117625,
      "text": "Keep the whole and the size of each part clear.",
      "source_sha256": "7de0d08ced37f8ccc850824d1ce1b46b4b55fde795d8689cea7e08f45879c64c"
    },
    {
      "start": 143.5,
      "end": 150.17933333333335,
      "text": "A five after one decimal place and a five after two decimal places do not have the same value.",
      "source_sha256": "d653752e44e73f66c043366490bce8dab6996801a051a33eb2a085de445e14cb"
    },
    {
      "start": 150.29933333333332,
      "end": 153.49179166666667,
      "text": "Five tenths is ten times five hundredths.",
      "source_sha256": "53a27cc0ef8ccbf6a2ca9c0930f412d5b1faed6af94b740c8fbf0c30220bf8a6"
    },
    {
      "start": 153.61179166666668,
      "end": 157.51975,
      "text": "Keep the same-sized whole in mind when you compare the parts.",
      "source_sha256": "81505253ac900d5bd69ef37442de4da108d1ff2cf9b30d7ad703b74e059770ea"
    },
    {
      "start": 157.9,
      "end": 161.640625,
      "text": "What is the value of the eight in 5.218?",
      "source_sha256": "7c9513d22a1afeae09635b8b65109f26d2218daef9f13364352c2400cce9264e"
    },
    {
      "start": 166.66666666666666,
      "end": 171.102625,
      "text": "The eight is in the thousandths place, so it represents eight thousandths.",
      "source_sha256": "0cf946d4b953bcf905cf067fe35f61f7393d6b18e6b16b357937553978bb3c50"
    },
    {
      "start": 171.46666666666667,
      "end": 174.925125,
      "text": "Try the page example: three point four five eight.",
      "source_sha256": "06c1d33fb1770538dbb001af85689538e4e81b2dceec7e54450faf2c9f837746"
    },
    {
      "start": 175.045125,
      "end": 180.17475,
      "text": "The five is in the hundredths place, so its value is zero point zero five.",
      "source_sha256": "be875b8374eea0a7e210cbccfc992d7ecda7106a3ab6fff84bc2c59a200ced48"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.29475,
      "end": 183.65220833333333,
      "text": "Remember: ones, tenths, hundredths, thousandths.",
      "source_sha256": "8df9d0963ba69fdffc2e2ec8f49f09c0109706b740f87c72113bde0d39201b78"
    },
    {
      "start": 183.77220833333334,
      "end": 189.93825,
      "text": "Every step right divides the place value by ten; every step left makes it ten times as much.",
      "source_sha256": "f797b54d98efcc31dfab8a4432760664c498b5d32de53699079561e6fb74e016"
    },
    {
      "start": 190.3,
      "end": 194.683,
      "text": "Our goal was to explain decimal place value through thousandths.",
      "source_sha256": "b74fca0db81c07faacf55f1ec7156ef597c5850ac6d145992f55e1ca0309d5ad"
    },
    {
      "start": 194.803,
      "end": 200.59591666666665,
      "text": "You can now explain your strategy, check the places carefully, and show why your answer makes sense.",
      "source_sha256": "72dfd21364e9d624c83db67254bc8dc050af51b190f2b4ce62944209b65f94f3"
    },
    {
      "start": 200.71591666666666,
      "end": 204.329,
      "text": "Choose a number of your own and explain it to someone nearby.",
      "source_sha256": "8a4ab057fdd20aec8c7fb04983dd47e828cf4a15c1ae1b639e36fafabc914bc3"
    },
    {
      "start": 204.449,
      "end": 207.63670833333333,
      "text": "Then try the lesson practice on Math Magic.",
      "source_sha256": "8e3256f16702541b9b60339c43e6f5367195f536f368fabc5ca7d94870395949"
    }
  ],
